> Puts back the old cells' attribute first. The positions run down column 1 (CursorIndex 1 to ColumnOneCount) and on down column 2.
> Witness: L1 6 (c x1).

$6A3A c UpKey ; 4, 9: the cursor up one file
> Witness: L1 2 (c x1).

@module launcher ; Running the chosen file: the BASIC's launch line, the bell, the fade, back to the loader
@about The menu does not load the file itself: it writes a TR-DOS command into line 1 of its own BASIC program (src/basic, LaunchLine $5D3B): RUN "name" for a BASIC file, GO TO "name" CODE for a 192-sector CODE file, puts the caller's I, HL', IY and SP back, Frames = 0 and CHARS = $3C00 (the ROM font), plays the bell, fades the screen and returns, IM 1, to the loader (src/basic, Loader $5D80), which clears its memory and returns to BASIC. Line 10's RUN then starts line 1: RANDOMIZE USR 15619: REM : RUN "name" hands the command to TR-DOS.

$6A3F c FireKey ; 5, 0, ENTER: run the file under the cursor (none with no files)
> C = "@" + CursorIndex: the letter of the file.
> Witness: L1 2 (c x2).

$6A51 c RunLetter ; Run the page's file with letter C (A for the first): write the launch line, restore the caller's state, bell, fade, return to the loader
> Returns at once when C is past the page's last file. Walks the catalogue from PagePointer $B3C1 counting the listed files; each entry passed has its first byte set to 1 (deleted), so the walk's SkipDeleted steps over it, and the chosen one gets its byte back. LaunchToken $5D4C = $F7 (RUN) for a B file, $EC (GO TO) for a 192-sector C file; the name's 8 bytes after the quote; after the closing quote a space or $AF (CODE). Frames = 0; I, HL', IY and SP from Start; Chars = $3C00; PlayBell $6E48; ExitFade $6E72; IM 1; EI; RET to the loader's $5DB7 (after its CALL MenuStart at $5DB4).
> Witness: L1 3 (c x3).
$6A5E RunNextEntry ; the next catalogue entry
$6A7A ; exactly 192 sectors ($C0): a 48K Magic snapshot. Vadim's comment reads 'length >= C000'; the test is CP $C0 with JR Z, equality only
$6A7E RunSkipEntry
$6A83 RunBasic ; a BASIC file: RUN
$6A89 RunCheckLetter ; is this the file with the letter?
$6AB4 RunWriteSuffix ; the suffix: a space or CODE

