@module stars
$6BA5 c TwinkleStar ; The twinkle at each frame: new randoms at TwinkleClock 0, erase at the end of a twinkle, a frame every 4th frame
> TwinkleClock $DEAC (+2 a frame; 32 frames a twinkle plus the 7 held frames at $3E: 39 frames a twinkle, lit 30 and dark 9, 156 a round of 4): 0: NewRandoms $6BAB. Bits 0-5 = $3E (the twinkle's last frame): EraseTwinkle without a new frame, and for 7 of 8 times TwinkleClock - 2 (TwinklePause $DEB0 counts): an 8-frame pause. Else every 4th frame (clock bits 0-2 = 2): DrawTwinkle $6BFD.
> Witness: L1 13931 (c x4).
$6BCB TwinkleEnd ; the end of a twinkle: the pause
$6BE7 TwinkleErase
$6BF5 TwinkleEvery4 ; every 4th frame

$6BAB c NewRandoms ; Fill Randoms $ADEC with 8 new bytes from R, the ROM's bytes and MainTick
$6BBC NewRandomNext
> Witness: L1 244 (c x4).

$6BFD c DrawTwinkle ; Erase the twinkle and draw its next frame at the place from Randoms
> The place: the pair Randoms[2n], [2n+1], n = TwinkleClock bits 6-7; CheckTwinkleSpot $6C56 refuses a place on the menu's text or off the screen (new randoms and again). EraseTwinkle $6C71 sets TwinkleAddr. The frame: TwinkleClock bits 3-4, counted down when bit 5 is set: frames 0, 1, 2, 3, 3, 2, 1, 0; ORed onto the screen, 16 rows of 2 bytes.
> Witness: L1 5864 (c x4).
$6C19 DrawTwinkleSprite ; LD A,(TwinkleClock): a RET while TwinkleStar only erases
$6C24 DrawTwinkleFrame
$6C39 DrawTwinkleRow ; OR the sprite onto the screen
$6C53 DrawTwinkleNext

$6C56 c CheckTwinkleSpot ; Carry set if the place (HL) is allowed: the low byte below $E0 and its column clear of the menu
$6C64 CheckSpotColumn
> Witness: L1 5864 (c x4).

$6C71 c EraseTwinkle ; TwinkleAddr = the place; copy its 16 rows of 2 bytes from ScreenCopy (the twinkle is erased)
