@module logo ; The ZYX logo: its glint and its reflection
@about The logo (Logo $A900, four 40x40 sprites; src/res/graphics/logo.png) is printed by DrawScreen; DrawReflection $6DC6 prints it upside down at the bottom. For the first 64 frames of every 256 LogoGlint $6D04 runs a diagonal red glint across the logo (the top one when Frames' high byte is even, the reflection when odd).

$6D04 c LogoGlint ; Frames 0-63 of every 256: the glint across the logo or its reflection
$6D1F GlintHalf ; Frames high byte bit 0: the glint on the logo (even) or on its reflection (odd)
$6D35 GlintStart
$6D3D GlintCornerLeft
$6D40 GlintCornerRight
$6D44 GlintStep
$6D53 GlintRowStart
$6D56 GlintRow
> At Frames low byte 0 the corner cells by the logo turn red (2). Then on every even frame up to 52 a glint step (26 steps): 5 rows, each row's three cells left of the step restored from ScreenCopy's attributes (RestoreGlintCells $6D6A) and three cells red, bright red, red drawn (DrawGlintRow $6D8A), mirrored about the screen's centre, the row above one cell further on.
> Witness: L1 13931 (c x4).

$6D6A c RestoreGlintCells ; Copy 3 attribute cells at the glint's column and their mirror image from ScreenCopy
> Witness: L1 7605 (c x4).

$6D8A c DrawGlintRow ; Draw the glint's 3 cells (red, bright red, red) at the column and the mirror image
> Witness: L1 7605 (c x4).

$6DAE c GlintRed ; (HL) = 2 (red ink) if HL's column is within the logo (6-25)
> Witness: L1 30420 (c x4).

$6DBA c GlintBright ; (HL) = $42 (bright red) if HL's column is within the logo
> Witness: L1 15210 (c x4).

$6DC6 c DrawReflection ; Print the logo upside down into ScreenCopy's bottom third and copy it to the screen
